.TH fdisk 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
fdisk \- show or edit a partition table
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fdisk
[\fB\-l\fR] \fIdevice\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fdisk
reads the MBR partition table of
.I device
and, without
.BR \-l ,
offers to change it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
List the table and exit, changing nothing.  This is the safe form and
the one to reach for.
.SH NOTES
The card built by the PC3 tools has three partitions: a FAT one for
exchanging files with a PC, the FUZIX root, and a small reserved one.
The layout is written when the card image is made, and there is very
little reason to change it on the machine.
.PP
Editing the table of the card you are running from does not move the
data on it.  Get it wrong and the filesystem is unreachable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfs (1),
.BR mount (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR fat (1)
